1
00:02:41,080 --> 00:02:42,640
My name is Da.

2
00:02:43,360 --> 00:02:46,760
Short for Lada, not Nada.

3
00:02:47,360 --> 00:02:48,520
What do you want?

4
00:02:49,120 --> 00:02:50,360
Revenge on you.

5
00:02:53,920 --> 00:02:55,080
Who's there?

6
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:56,960
Wee?

7
00:02:57,040 --> 00:02:58,280
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Wee.</font></font></i>

8
00:02:58,360 --> 00:02:59,560
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Did Korn see you?</font></font></i>

9
00:03:00,160 --> 00:03:02,240
-I hid just in time.
-Did you get it?

10
00:03:03,120 --> 00:03:03,960
Yeah.

11
00:03:04,040 --> 00:03:06,440
To move abroad with me.

12
00:03:07,040 --> 00:03:09,080
I want to finally start a new life.

13
00:03:11,480 --> 00:03:14,440
I know everything now. Stop pretending.

14
00:03:14,520 --> 00:03:16,840
Just because I'm not Ms. Nada's real son,

15
00:03:16,920 --> 00:03:18,480
do you really have to hate me so much?

16
00:03:19,080 --> 00:03:20,760
You still don't realize
what you've done wrong?

17
00:03:22,080 --> 00:03:23,200
Don't worry.

18
00:03:24,160 --> 00:03:27,280
I'll definitely speak up
when I get the chance.

19
00:03:45,600 --> 00:03:47,320
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">You really do look like Rawich.</font></font></i>

20
00:03:47,920 --> 00:03:51,160
Who's Rawich?

21
00:03:51,800 --> 00:03:53,120
My former secretary.

22
00:03:54,600 --> 00:03:57,320
Nada's husband. He died a long time ago.

23
00:04:00,160 --> 00:04:01,280
Who named you?

24
00:04:02,720 --> 00:04:03,760
My mother.

25
00:04:04,920 --> 00:04:06,640
Your names are so similar.

26
00:04:23,920 --> 00:04:24,800
Wee.

27
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:28,040
I'm serious.

28
00:04:28,880 --> 00:04:30,480
If you want to get everything back,

29
00:04:32,200 --> 00:04:33,720
we can't do this on our own.

30
00:04:36,640 --> 00:04:38,080
We need to find someone to help us.

31
00:04:39,960 --> 00:04:42,080
Or we need to gather more evidence first.

32
00:05:09,840 --> 00:05:11,960
-Resign?
-Yes, sir.

33
00:05:12,840 --> 00:05:15,240
Is something wrong? Why are you resigning?

34
00:05:15,320 --> 00:05:16,960
I need to take care of Ms. La…

35
00:05:18,120 --> 00:05:19,560
Ms. Nada.

36
00:05:20,240 --> 00:05:22,960
What's wrong with Nada? Why does she
need someone to look after her?

37
00:05:23,040 --> 00:05:24,640
There's nothing wrong with her.

38
00:05:24,720 --> 00:05:28,040
She just wants to retire
and move to America.

39
00:05:28,120 --> 00:05:31,400
So she asked me to go with her.

40
00:05:33,160 --> 00:05:36,280
Wait. Don't tell me you and Nada…

41
00:05:37,160 --> 00:05:38,000
Yes, sir.

42
00:06:00,560 --> 00:06:01,760
Ms. Alyssa.

43
00:06:02,920 --> 00:06:05,760
Why haven't you told my father
about Ms. Lada?

44
00:06:06,960 --> 00:06:09,920
Well, Mr. Nimit is ill.

45
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:11,600
I don't want to stress him out.

46
00:06:12,680 --> 00:06:14,640
Then you shouldn't have done it
in the first place.

47
00:06:16,360 --> 00:06:18,360
This will all be over soon.

48
00:06:18,960 --> 00:06:21,600
Over? How?

49
00:06:21,680 --> 00:06:24,960
With you and Ms. Lada
living happily ever after,

50
00:06:25,040 --> 00:06:28,240
while everyone else suffers
for what you two have done?

51
00:06:29,320 --> 00:06:31,320
You'd better stay out of this, Ms. Alyssa.

52
00:06:31,400 --> 00:06:34,800
I can't stay out of it. What you two did

53
00:06:34,880 --> 00:06:37,280
has hurt people
who had nothing to do with it.

54
00:06:37,880 --> 00:06:39,040
What do you expect me to do?

55
00:06:40,400 --> 00:06:42,960
Turn myself in and go to prison?

56
00:06:43,560 --> 00:06:44,880
Can you?

57
00:07:10,960 --> 00:07:14,360
What's gotten into you now?
I thought we'd settled this.

58
00:07:16,440 --> 00:07:18,960
Or don't you want to come with me?

59
00:07:19,040 --> 00:07:20,280
If we're going to leave,

60
00:07:20,360 --> 00:07:21,800
can't we just go now?

61
00:07:22,920 --> 00:07:24,720
Leave everything behind and go.

62
00:07:24,800 --> 00:07:25,800
No.

63
00:07:26,560 --> 00:07:29,360
I have to see my plan through to the end.

64
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:32,280
Otherwise, I'll never

65
00:07:32,360 --> 00:07:33,920
rest in peace.

66
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:36,680
Whether you come or not is up to you.

67
00:07:37,640 --> 00:07:41,160
But I'm sticking to my original plan.

68
00:07:51,880 --> 00:07:52,640
Where are you going?

69
00:07:56,800 --> 00:07:58,160
I asked you where you're going.

70
00:07:58,920 --> 00:08:00,560
You can't leave yet.

71
00:08:01,160 --> 00:08:03,320
You have to transfer
the Tayawat assets to me first.

72
00:08:06,720 --> 00:08:07,800
What did you say?

73
00:08:10,680 --> 00:08:11,920
The assets?

74
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:13,080
Yes.

75
00:08:14,240 --> 00:08:18,680
The company shares, the cash,
everything the Tayawats own.

76
00:08:24,280 --> 00:08:26,120
Are you joking, Phakorn?

77
00:08:26,920 --> 00:08:29,480
Don't be so greedy.

78
00:08:30,280 --> 00:08:34,480
You're lucky I haven't
reported you for fraud.

79
00:08:35,559 --> 00:08:37,440
Go ahead. Do it.

80
00:08:38,039 --> 00:08:39,840
You think I want to be here?

81
00:08:39,919 --> 00:08:41,960
If it weren't for that damn disease,

82
00:08:42,039 --> 00:08:43,360
I wouldn't even be here.

83
00:08:44,039 --> 00:08:46,120
I wouldn't have had to give up my old life

84
00:08:46,720 --> 00:08:49,640
or get dragged into
your stupid revenge scheme.

85
00:08:50,600 --> 00:08:52,840
You see me as nothing but a pawn.

86
00:08:52,920 --> 00:08:54,360
But I'm human too.

87
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:58,920
I have a life, a heart, and feelings.

88
00:08:59,640 --> 00:09:00,480
So what?

89
00:09:02,080 --> 00:09:04,480
You chose to be here.

90
00:09:04,560 --> 00:09:06,760
You chose to be my pawn.

91
00:09:06,840 --> 00:09:08,680
I never forced you.

92
00:09:10,360 --> 00:09:12,200
You've ruined my life.

93
00:09:13,360 --> 00:09:15,520
You ruined it yourself.

94
00:09:17,520 --> 00:09:18,960
I can't turn back now.

95
00:09:22,440 --> 00:09:24,440
I'm not giving you a thing.

96
00:09:24,520 --> 00:09:26,560
If anyone gets anything,

97
00:09:26,640 --> 00:09:28,360
it should be Rawee.

98
00:09:28,440 --> 00:09:30,760
Not a fake son like you!

99
00:09:30,840 --> 00:09:32,760
And you're just as fake a mother!

100
00:09:33,360 --> 00:09:34,760
I'd love to see

101
00:09:34,840 --> 00:09:38,440
how you'll live once everyone
finds out who you really are.

102
00:09:39,040 --> 00:09:40,040
Are you threatening me?

103
00:09:40,720 --> 00:09:44,520
I'm not threatening you.
And don't think I'm some idiot

104
00:09:44,600 --> 00:09:48,600
you can push around.
I'm capable of more than you think.

105
00:09:51,120 --> 00:09:53,600
I know you've been meeting

106
00:09:53,680 --> 00:09:56,560
with a rival company

107
00:09:57,400 --> 00:09:58,840
and acquiring all those shares.

108
00:10:01,680 --> 00:10:02,840
What do you want?

109
00:10:05,200 --> 00:10:07,520
All the company shares you've acquired.

110
00:10:08,920 --> 00:10:10,000
I want them all.

111
00:10:20,640 --> 00:10:21,640
Dream on.

112
00:10:28,800 --> 00:10:29,960
Damn it!

113
00:10:40,800 --> 00:10:41,840
No wonder

114
00:10:42,560 --> 00:10:46,440
you're not real brothers.
You're nothing alike.

115
00:10:48,080 --> 00:10:49,680
If you're planning to kill me,

116
00:10:50,600 --> 00:10:53,400
go ahead. I'm not afraid.

117
00:10:54,240 --> 00:10:56,320
But you'd better hurry.

118
00:10:56,920 --> 00:10:58,480
Because the moment I find proof

119
00:10:58,560 --> 00:11:00,960
that you were involved in someone's death,

120
00:11:02,320 --> 00:11:03,640
I'll make sure you go to jail.

121
00:12:35,280 --> 00:12:36,960
NO CALLER ID

122
00:12:39,320 --> 00:12:40,320
Hello?

123
00:12:43,360 --> 00:12:44,720
It's Rawee speaking.

124
00:12:48,760 --> 00:12:49,640
Who is this?

125
00:12:50,240 --> 00:12:51,200
It's me, Rawee.

126
00:13:03,320 --> 00:13:05,040
That's not funny. Don't joke about this.

127
00:13:06,200 --> 00:13:07,560
I'm not joking.

128
00:13:21,440 --> 00:13:22,720
It really is you.

129
00:13:25,040 --> 00:13:27,480
A fisherman saved my life.

130
00:13:27,560 --> 00:13:29,200
That's how I survived.

131
00:13:29,280 --> 00:13:30,680
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Can you come and meet me?</font></font></i>

132
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:33,160
Where are you?

133
00:13:35,600 --> 00:13:37,720
There's a motorcycle following you, right?

134
00:13:50,400 --> 00:13:54,280
That's my friend Kongphob.
Just follow him.

135
00:14:29,600 --> 00:14:31,360
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">That's what Uncle Thamrong told me.</font></font></i>

136
00:14:35,840 --> 00:14:37,760
That's what Thong told me too.

137
00:14:39,360 --> 00:14:42,000
Korn caused you
to fall off the cliff, didn't he?

138
00:14:57,000 --> 00:14:58,040
He didn't mean to.

139
00:15:02,640 --> 00:15:03,480
Really?

140
00:15:06,280 --> 00:15:08,840
You need to wake up already.

141
00:15:09,960 --> 00:15:12,560
Korn wants you out of the way.

142
00:15:12,640 --> 00:15:14,800
He's working with Ms. Lada.

143
00:15:16,760 --> 00:15:20,400
When will you stop
blindly defending your brother?

144
00:15:24,320 --> 00:15:26,960
That sweet little boy you raised

145
00:15:27,840 --> 00:15:29,480
died in the operating room.

146
00:15:32,880 --> 00:15:34,960
I'm trying to find a way
to bring him back.

147
00:15:35,760 --> 00:15:38,040
Deep down, Korn isn't a bad person.

148
00:15:41,200 --> 00:15:43,000
Then why did you want to see me?

149
00:15:44,600 --> 00:15:45,520
Ms. Alyssa.

150
00:15:47,080 --> 00:15:49,840
Could you ask Uncle Thamrong
to tell the police the truth

151
00:15:50,520 --> 00:15:52,720
about me and Ms. Lada?

152
00:15:54,440 --> 00:15:55,840
I have to put a stop to all this

153
00:15:56,480 --> 00:15:58,480
before Korn gets in any deeper.

154
00:16:20,320 --> 00:16:23,400
Da, are you still mad at me?

155
00:16:25,600 --> 00:16:28,360
I just feel guilty about Rawee.

156
00:16:29,880 --> 00:16:33,760
I've already decided
that once this is all over,

157
00:16:33,840 --> 00:16:35,680
I'll give Rawee
a share of the inheritance.

158
00:16:36,280 --> 00:16:40,000
But then again, Rawee was unlucky
to get involved with Phakorn.

159
00:16:42,440 --> 00:16:45,920
You think Phakorn
was behind Rawee's death?

160
00:16:47,200 --> 00:16:49,120
He's no ordinary boy.

161
00:16:49,200 --> 00:16:51,960
Who would've thought jealousy

162
00:16:52,040 --> 00:16:53,760
could drive someone to do anything?

163
00:16:57,800 --> 00:16:59,480
Don't say what you said
this morning again.

164
00:17:00,480 --> 00:17:02,120
We've been through so much.

165
00:17:03,040 --> 00:17:06,440
Just hang in there a little longer,
and it'll all be over.

166
00:17:25,520 --> 00:17:27,280
-Hello.
-Hello.

167
00:17:32,280 --> 00:17:33,320
What is it?

168
00:17:34,160 --> 00:17:36,560
Are you Mr. Thamrong Wongphisit?

169
00:17:37,400 --> 00:17:39,960
Yes, that's me.
Is something wrong, Officer?

170
00:17:40,600 --> 00:17:41,720
Here.

171
00:17:42,800 --> 00:17:44,720
We have further evidence

172
00:17:44,800 --> 00:17:47,720
linking you to the death
of Ms. Pimpa Tayawat.

173
00:17:48,320 --> 00:17:49,840
Please come in to give a statement.

174
00:18:05,760 --> 00:18:08,960
Wee, Mr. Thamrong's been arrested.

175
00:18:10,920 --> 00:18:12,320
What for?

176
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:16,560
He's suspected of murdering Ms. Pimpa.

177
00:18:17,200 --> 00:18:19,600
Are you kidding me? Thamrong?

178
00:18:20,560 --> 00:18:22,880
The news says they have evidence too.

179
00:18:22,960 --> 00:18:24,920
There's dashcam footage

180
00:18:25,000 --> 00:18:28,480
showing Thamrong getting into the car
before Ms. Pimpa died.

181
00:18:29,520 --> 00:18:31,760
Why would he do something like that?

182
00:18:31,840 --> 00:18:34,560
He has nothing to do with that family.

183
00:18:45,960 --> 00:18:48,320
-Have they finished questioning him?
-Not yet.

184
00:18:49,440 --> 00:18:51,920
I'd like to speak
to Uncle Thamrong privately.

185
00:18:52,560 --> 00:18:54,360
Just a moment. I'll arrange it.

186
00:19:03,600 --> 00:19:04,720
LAWYER TONG

187
00:19:08,280 --> 00:19:09,240
Yes?

188
00:19:12,520 --> 00:19:14,280
Thanks.

189
00:19:16,680 --> 00:19:18,320
What did Lawyer Tong say?

190
00:19:18,400 --> 00:19:20,200
They're still questioning him.

191
00:19:21,680 --> 00:19:25,320
What? Isn't Ms. Nada
doing anything to help him?

192
00:19:25,920 --> 00:19:28,560
If you hadn't sent Lawyer Tong,

193
00:19:28,640 --> 00:19:31,400
Thamrong would've been all on his own.

194
00:19:32,360 --> 00:19:36,000
I thought they were madly in love
and planning to move abroad together.

195
00:19:37,640 --> 00:19:39,960
Wait. What if…

196
00:19:41,920 --> 00:19:43,800
she's been using him?

197
00:19:47,720 --> 00:19:50,280
Did Uncle Thamrong confess like I asked?

198
00:19:52,520 --> 00:19:53,480
No.

199
00:19:55,720 --> 00:19:58,360
He's afraid Ms. Lada
will get dragged into it too.

200
00:19:59,800 --> 00:20:02,040
You'll have to find
other evidence to prove it.

201
00:20:04,040 --> 00:20:04,920
Okay.

202
00:20:15,960 --> 00:20:16,960
What now?

203
00:20:20,840 --> 00:20:22,840
Uncle Thamrong won't confess.

204
00:20:23,440 --> 00:20:25,200
So he really got arrested, huh?

205
00:20:25,800 --> 00:20:29,080
Ms. Alyssa's got guts,
turning in her own uncle.

206
00:20:30,320 --> 00:20:32,800
-He's not her real uncle.
-Still!

207
00:20:34,280 --> 00:20:37,480
She must really like you
to go this far to help you.

208
00:20:38,280 --> 00:20:42,160
You're talking nonsense.
Maybe she just believes in justice.

209
00:20:46,040 --> 00:20:47,440
So what are you gonna do now?

210
00:20:47,520 --> 00:20:49,440
If Mr. Thamrong won't talk,

211
00:20:50,400 --> 00:20:52,240
is there anyone else who knows about this?

212
00:21:32,720 --> 00:21:33,720
Wee!

213
00:21:39,360 --> 00:21:41,200
Is that really you?

214
00:21:42,480 --> 00:21:44,960
I'm not imagining things, am I?

215
00:21:48,760 --> 00:21:49,800
It's me, Mom.

216
00:21:51,120 --> 00:21:53,680
It's really me. I'm still alive.

217
00:21:54,800 --> 00:21:58,200
Where have you been all this time?
Why didn't you contact me?

218
00:21:58,800 --> 00:22:00,240
Do you have any idea

219
00:22:00,320 --> 00:22:03,800
how worried I've been? Huh?

220
00:22:08,080 --> 00:22:10,160
Wee.

221
00:22:14,160 --> 00:22:16,160
I'm sorry I had to keep this from you.

222
00:22:17,920 --> 00:22:20,120
I had to do it for Korn.

223
00:22:27,440 --> 00:22:28,880
Please don't tell anyone yet,

224
00:22:30,120 --> 00:22:32,600
especially Korn. Korn mustn't find out.

225
00:22:34,440 --> 00:22:35,760
Korn's going down the wrong path.

226
00:22:37,120 --> 00:22:39,960
We have to stop him
before he gets in any deeper, Mom.

227
00:22:43,720 --> 00:22:45,880
It's like someone replaced his brain
with someone else's.

228
00:22:45,960 --> 00:22:48,640
No one in our family
has ever been like this.

229
00:22:58,840 --> 00:23:02,840
I'm sorry I couldn't save Wee.

230
00:23:03,880 --> 00:23:05,080
It's okay, son.

231
00:23:07,600 --> 00:23:09,720
You did your best.

232
00:23:10,520 --> 00:23:12,520
Wee fell off the cliff…

233
00:23:17,200 --> 00:23:19,440
because he was trying to save me.

234
00:23:21,920 --> 00:23:24,280
Korn caused you to fall
off the cliff, didn't he?

235
00:23:29,760 --> 00:23:31,880
You wouldn't lie to me, would you?

236
00:23:34,000 --> 00:23:36,080
I want to hear it from Korn himself too.

237
00:23:58,360 --> 00:24:00,960
Mr. Korn!

238
00:24:01,040 --> 00:24:03,040
Mr. Korn, what's wrong? Mr. Korn!

239
00:24:03,120 --> 00:24:06,160
Are you okay? Get up slowly, Mr. Korn.

240
00:24:07,480 --> 00:24:10,000
Mr. Korn, sit down first.

241
00:24:15,680 --> 00:24:18,000
Would you like me to call an ambulance?

242
00:24:19,520 --> 00:24:20,520
No.

243
00:24:21,720 --> 00:24:24,160
-Get my medicine from the bedside drawer.
-Yes, sir.

244
00:24:24,240 --> 00:24:25,840
-It's in a white bottle.
-Right away.

245
00:24:49,360 --> 00:24:51,640
Yes, thank you very much.

246
00:24:51,720 --> 00:24:54,800
Please call me if you hear anything.

247
00:24:57,320 --> 00:24:58,720
Is this about Mr. Thamrong?

248
00:25:00,280 --> 00:25:02,080
Is there anything I can do to help?

249
00:25:02,840 --> 00:25:06,840
No. I don't want to seem too involved,
or Mr. Nimit might get suspicious.

250
00:25:07,760 --> 00:25:11,160
Right now, I need
to sort out the shares first.

251
00:25:12,880 --> 00:25:13,720
Yes, ma'am.

252
00:25:26,640 --> 00:25:29,720
POWER OF ATTORNEY FOR SHARE MANAGEMENT

253
00:25:32,040 --> 00:25:33,600
Don't fall asleep yet, Father.

254
00:25:35,040 --> 00:25:36,560
Sign the document for me first.

255
00:25:55,160 --> 00:25:56,320
PRAJAK TAYAWAT, CHAIRMAN

256
00:26:04,040 --> 00:26:05,280
-Taddao.
-Yes.

257
00:26:05,360 --> 00:26:06,520
Take care of this for me.

258
00:26:07,120 --> 00:26:08,440
Of course, Ms. Lada.

259
00:26:20,360 --> 00:26:22,080
So you were behind Pimpa's death,

260
00:26:23,160 --> 00:26:24,800
weren't you?

261
00:26:44,080 --> 00:26:45,200
Look at you.

262
00:26:57,680 --> 00:26:58,520
Hello?

263
00:26:59,360 --> 00:27:01,160
The DNA results are in?

264
00:27:02,160 --> 00:27:04,200
Is Phakorn Nada's son?

265
00:27:06,720 --> 00:27:09,920
He isn't? No match at all?

266
00:27:11,720 --> 00:27:12,840
Are you sure?

267
00:27:13,440 --> 00:27:15,520
What about Rawee?

268
00:27:15,600 --> 00:27:17,760
Does his DNA match Nada's?

269
00:27:20,280 --> 00:27:21,200
No?

270
00:27:22,640 --> 00:27:23,680
Alright.

271
00:27:24,400 --> 00:27:25,680
I see.

272
00:27:27,600 --> 00:27:29,400
Where are the results now?

273
00:27:32,800 --> 00:27:36,320
You left them with…? Oh, okay.

274
00:27:36,400 --> 00:27:39,760
I'll come get them right away. Bye.

275
00:27:49,080 --> 00:27:51,360
Mother and son both put on quite an act.

276
00:27:52,360 --> 00:27:54,560
Just you wait. This time,

277
00:27:55,440 --> 00:27:58,000
I'll bring you down, Nada.

278
00:28:37,040 --> 00:28:40,280
THAMRONG - GET RID OF PIMPA

279
00:28:44,120 --> 00:28:47,080
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">If you have something to confess,</font></font></i>
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">out with it.</font></font></i>

280
00:28:48,880 --> 00:28:51,280
Did you secretly have my blood
tested for DNA?

281
00:28:52,400 --> 00:28:56,600
Yes. And now I know you're not Nada's son.

282
00:29:01,240 --> 00:29:04,760
My father will hear about this.

283
00:29:09,080 --> 00:29:10,360
Get out now.

284
00:29:13,920 --> 00:29:16,320
Hey! What are you doing?

285
00:29:18,040 --> 00:29:19,840
Stop! Stop right now!

286
00:29:22,720 --> 00:29:24,080
Don't!

287
00:29:26,200 --> 00:29:27,240
Stop!

288
00:29:28,440 --> 00:29:29,640
Hey!

289
00:29:30,760 --> 00:29:31,800
Stop!

290
00:29:36,920 --> 00:29:38,120
No!

291
00:29:57,760 --> 00:29:59,520
Uh, hey!

292
00:29:59,600 --> 00:30:01,920
Aunt!

293
00:30:03,000 --> 00:30:03,920
Aunt!

294
00:30:15,520 --> 00:30:16,840
She's still alive.

295
00:31:10,320 --> 00:31:12,960
How can you be so cruel?

296
00:31:14,400 --> 00:31:16,360
Like father, like daughter, I suppose.

297
00:31:18,320 --> 00:31:22,960
You burned everyone in the village alive,

298
00:31:23,560 --> 00:31:26,320
then used your money and power
to cover it up

299
00:31:26,400 --> 00:31:28,120
and make it look like you did nothing.

300
00:31:31,640 --> 00:31:34,520
Come to think of it, Father,

301
00:31:35,120 --> 00:31:36,880
you're far more ruthless than I am.

302
00:31:38,480 --> 00:31:39,840
Don't be shocked just yet.

303
00:31:40,440 --> 00:31:42,320
There's plenty more to come.

304
00:31:43,960 --> 00:31:47,240
And do you know who's next?

305
00:31:48,520 --> 00:31:50,840
Your youngest son.

306
00:31:52,680 --> 00:31:55,240
He set up a fake stock trading site
and scammed people.

307
00:31:56,080 --> 00:31:58,360
Now he's on the run.

308
00:31:59,200 --> 00:32:00,200
Once they catch him,

309
00:32:00,840 --> 00:32:04,400
he's going straight to prison.
Don't worry, Father.

310
00:32:05,240 --> 00:32:08,920
I won't let any of this
tarnish the company's reputation.

311
00:32:12,480 --> 00:32:14,120
Excuse me.

312
00:32:15,920 --> 00:32:19,840
I'll be going now, Father.
I won't be staying for dinner.

313
00:32:19,920 --> 00:32:21,560
I have a lot to take care of.

314
00:32:27,480 --> 00:32:30,640
Let me check your blood pressure.
Excuse me.

315
00:33:16,920 --> 00:33:19,520
These documents
are from the police station.

316
00:33:21,960 --> 00:33:23,520
I'm counting on you, Lawyer Tong.

317
00:33:24,360 --> 00:33:25,360
Yes, sir.

318
00:33:25,960 --> 00:33:29,360
I'll call you when I have an update.

319
00:33:31,360 --> 00:33:33,200
I'll be going now. Goodbye, sir.

320
00:33:50,960 --> 00:33:52,440
Why was Lawyer Tong here?

321
00:34:01,120 --> 00:34:02,120
Is something wrong?

322
00:34:09,440 --> 00:34:11,440
Uncle Thamrong died in prison last night.

323
00:34:13,159 --> 00:34:14,560
How is that possible?

324
00:34:15,440 --> 00:34:17,960
Lawyer Tong said it was suicide.

325
00:34:19,080 --> 00:34:20,400
That can't be true.

326
00:34:22,120 --> 00:34:23,760
I don't believe it either.

327
00:34:24,679 --> 00:34:26,800
I think someone killed him
to keep him quiet.

328
00:34:28,320 --> 00:34:29,159
I see.

329
00:38:36,120 --> 00:38:38,640
PHAKORN

330
00:38:42,960 --> 00:38:43,960
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Yes, Mom?</font></font></i>

331
00:38:44,040 --> 00:38:46,000
I want you to come to a funeral with me.

332
00:38:46,600 --> 00:38:47,960
Whose funeral?

333
00:38:48,840 --> 00:38:50,320
Well, it's not Wee's.

334
00:38:51,440 --> 00:38:53,720
Can't you ever speak nicely to me, Mom?

335
00:38:55,720 --> 00:38:57,600
Uncle Thamrong died last night.

336
00:39:14,280 --> 00:39:18,480
Mr. Thamrong's dead? How is that possible?

337
00:40:19,480 --> 00:40:20,560
Are you ready?

338
00:40:23,160 --> 00:40:24,160
Ready for what?

339
00:40:26,520 --> 00:40:28,800
To move abroad with me.

340
00:40:29,440 --> 00:40:31,720
I'll get everything wrapped up
as soon as possible.

341
00:40:34,560 --> 00:40:36,520
I want to finally start a new life.

342
00:41:49,680 --> 00:41:50,960
I need to talk to you.

343
00:41:59,400 --> 00:42:01,920
Where's Ms. Nada? I can't get hold of her.

344
00:42:04,200 --> 00:42:05,680
I don't know either.

345
00:42:08,160 --> 00:42:09,280
Should I believe you?

346
00:42:10,520 --> 00:42:13,640
Believe what you want.
I've been trying to reach her myself.

347
00:42:15,160 --> 00:42:18,680
Good. At least she can say goodbye
to the man she loved.

348
00:42:21,840 --> 00:42:22,880
What do you know?

349
00:42:23,960 --> 00:42:25,240
You really don't know

350
00:42:26,440 --> 00:42:28,640
Ms. Nada and Uncle Thamrong were together?

351
00:42:33,920 --> 00:42:35,000
And you don't know

352
00:42:36,440 --> 00:42:37,800
the woman you call Mom

353
00:42:39,480 --> 00:42:40,680
isn't the real Ms. Nada, either?

354
00:42:56,760 --> 00:43:00,080
Excuse me. Could you let me in?

355
00:43:41,720 --> 00:43:43,800
I don't believe you killed yourself.

356
00:43:46,000 --> 00:43:47,480
You were a reasonable man.

357
00:43:48,400 --> 00:43:50,560
You always knew how to handle problems.

358
00:43:52,560 --> 00:43:55,800
I know you'd never run
from your problems in such a foolish way.

359
00:43:57,840 --> 00:44:00,000
I'll find the culprit
and bring them to justice.

360
00:44:12,720 --> 00:44:13,600
Whoa!

361
00:44:14,240 --> 00:44:15,720
I'm not dead.

362
00:44:26,720 --> 00:44:28,360
What's all this about?

363
00:44:39,280 --> 00:44:40,880
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Wee is safe now.</font></font></i>

364
00:44:42,160 --> 00:44:43,440
I went to see him.

365
00:44:43,520 --> 00:44:47,640
Really? Ms. Lada will be so happy
when she finds out.

366
00:44:48,880 --> 00:44:52,200
But no one can know yet.
He doesn't want anyone to know he's alive.

367
00:44:53,160 --> 00:44:54,360
Because of Korn?

368
00:44:56,720 --> 00:44:57,960
Uncle Thamrong.

369
00:44:59,040 --> 00:45:02,040
I'm the one who reported you
to the police.

370
00:45:08,400 --> 00:45:09,400
It's alright.

371
00:45:11,200 --> 00:45:13,360
This was bound to happen sooner or later.

372
00:45:15,120 --> 00:45:17,160
I was prepared for it.

373
00:45:21,760 --> 00:45:23,680
I'll be straightforward with you.

374
00:45:26,000 --> 00:45:27,880
Wee wants you

375
00:45:27,960 --> 00:45:30,720
to tell the police
the truth about Ms. Lada.

376
00:45:36,440 --> 00:45:37,440
Well…

377
00:45:38,280 --> 00:45:39,680
This is your chance

378
00:45:40,760 --> 00:45:42,960
to make amends

379
00:45:43,040 --> 00:45:45,360
for your part
in the deaths of his parents.

380
00:45:50,880 --> 00:45:53,720
Even if I confess, it won't be enough.

381
00:45:54,800 --> 00:45:56,560
Not as long as Ms. Lada refuses to stop.

382
00:45:58,200 --> 00:46:01,440
Isn't there any way to make Ms. Lada stop?

383
00:46:04,600 --> 00:46:06,200
She has suffered a great deal.

384
00:46:07,880 --> 00:46:10,880
You could say revenge has become
her whole reason for living.

385
00:46:14,240 --> 00:46:16,360
But her revenge is hurting people

386
00:46:16,440 --> 00:46:18,160
who had nothing to do with it.

387
00:46:19,040 --> 00:46:22,440
If she wants revenge on Mr. Prajak,
she should take it out on him alone.

388
00:46:25,200 --> 00:46:26,840
I just don't understand

389
00:46:27,720 --> 00:46:29,920
how you fell into her trap, Uncle.

390
00:46:34,240 --> 00:46:38,000
I guess I did fall into her trap.

391
00:46:41,480 --> 00:46:43,240
Without your help,

392
00:46:44,920 --> 00:46:47,080
Ms. Lada couldn't have gotten this far.

393
00:46:58,840 --> 00:47:00,960
These documents
are from the police station.

394
00:47:05,120 --> 00:47:06,400
I'm counting on you, Lawyer Tong.

395
00:47:08,520 --> 00:47:11,760
Yes, sir. I'll call you

396
00:47:11,840 --> 00:47:13,520
when I have an update.

397
00:47:15,160 --> 00:47:17,240
I'll be going now. Goodbye, sir.

398
00:47:37,160 --> 00:47:39,960
So faking his death was your idea?

399
00:47:40,920 --> 00:47:44,000
Yes. I wanted to see

400
00:47:44,800 --> 00:47:48,280
what Ms. Lada would do
without Uncle Thamrong.

401
00:47:48,880 --> 00:47:50,480
Especially now that Mr. Prajak is awake.

402
00:47:53,040 --> 00:47:57,040
I guess I overestimated my importance.

403
00:47:58,160 --> 00:48:01,080
Maybe I'm not as important
to Lada's plan as I thought.

404
00:48:04,960 --> 00:48:06,640
Don't feel bad, Uncle.

405
00:48:07,520 --> 00:48:10,920
For now, you need
to stay away from Ms. Lada.

406
00:48:11,600 --> 00:48:15,880
Whatever she does from here on,
please don't get involved again.

407
00:48:16,640 --> 00:48:20,240
I want you to be Wee's trump card.

408
00:48:23,760 --> 00:48:25,280
What about the case?

409
00:48:26,720 --> 00:48:29,240
I put up collateral
to bail Uncle Thamrong out.

410
00:48:29,320 --> 00:48:31,440
Then I had the lawyer help stage his death

411
00:48:31,520 --> 00:48:33,720
and arranged a fake funeral.

412
00:48:34,720 --> 00:48:38,160
Could you accept it
if Ms. Lada ended up in prison?

413
00:48:39,320 --> 00:48:40,400
Rawee, I…

414
00:48:41,600 --> 00:48:43,800
I'm sorry. I'm truly sorry

415
00:48:46,120 --> 00:48:49,080
for my part in your parents' deaths.

416
00:48:51,000 --> 00:48:53,840
If you'd known something terrible
would happen to my parents,

417
00:48:55,040 --> 00:48:56,880
you wouldn't have helped Ms. Lada,
would you?

418
00:49:01,360 --> 00:49:05,000
And I hope Ms. Lada never thought
her actions would cause

419
00:49:05,960 --> 00:49:08,200
her sister
and brother-in-law's deaths either.

420
00:49:11,440 --> 00:49:12,520
Are you okay, Wee?

421
00:49:13,960 --> 00:49:15,040
I'm okay.

422
00:49:16,760 --> 00:49:19,960
Maybe I don't feel that sad

423
00:49:21,520 --> 00:49:23,280
because I wasn't that close to my parents.

424
00:49:24,720 --> 00:49:27,920
But I also robbed you
of the life you deserved.

425
00:49:31,280 --> 00:49:33,800
I'm sorry. I'm truly sorry.

426
00:49:39,760 --> 00:49:41,360
It's in the past, Uncle.

427
00:49:42,560 --> 00:49:44,200
There's no point dwelling on it.

428
00:49:45,360 --> 00:49:47,520
For now,

429
00:49:48,400 --> 00:49:52,040
let's work together
to find a way to set things right.

430
00:49:53,200 --> 00:49:55,160
I just hope we can stop all this

431
00:49:55,960 --> 00:49:58,560
before Ms. Lada and Korn
do anything worse.

432
00:50:02,360 --> 00:50:03,200
Thank you so much.

433
00:50:07,080 --> 00:50:10,920
Those who've done wrong are lucky
to be loved so much.

434
00:50:15,480 --> 00:50:19,440
You wouldn't have faked your deaths
if you didn't care about them, right?

435
00:50:24,200 --> 00:50:26,600
Come to think of it, I'm talking

436
00:50:26,680 --> 00:50:28,640
to two spirits right now.

437
00:50:29,840 --> 00:50:31,240
Two ghosts, you could say.

438
00:50:35,080 --> 00:50:39,040
I think if we gather
enough evidence or witnesses,

439
00:50:39,600 --> 00:50:43,120
you could reclaim your place
as a Tayawat heir.

440
00:50:46,560 --> 00:50:48,960
I still don't know
how to prove who I really am.

441
00:50:52,080 --> 00:50:54,600
Your paternal grandparents
are still alive, aren't they?

442
00:50:57,280 --> 00:51:00,640
Uh, well…

443
00:51:00,720 --> 00:51:02,760
I did a little research.

444
00:51:03,480 --> 00:51:06,520
Their DNA can also
help prove your identity,

445
00:51:06,600 --> 00:51:08,640
even though the percentage
of shared DNA is lower.

446
00:51:25,960 --> 00:51:26,960
Thank you.

447
00:51:28,600 --> 00:51:29,600
For what?

448
00:51:30,960 --> 00:51:34,560
Good question. I don't
even know where to start.

449
00:51:34,640 --> 00:51:35,840
There's so much to thank you for.

450
00:51:37,640 --> 00:51:39,360
I haven't done anything.

451
00:51:41,200 --> 00:51:42,800
You've been helping me all along, Alyssa.

452
00:51:43,920 --> 00:51:46,680
Thank you for still being here for me.

453
00:51:49,880 --> 00:51:52,320
What I've done is nothing

454
00:51:52,400 --> 00:51:54,920
compared to what you've done for me.

455
00:51:56,320 --> 00:51:59,720
You've gotten into trouble
because of me over and over again.

456
00:52:01,680 --> 00:52:04,040
Are you helping me
because you feel guilty?

457
00:52:05,800 --> 00:52:06,680
No.

458
00:52:08,320 --> 00:52:10,760
I'm helping because I want to.

459
00:52:13,680 --> 00:52:15,680
I want you to be happy, Wee.

460
00:52:22,280 --> 00:52:26,200
Still, you need to be careful too.
You know that, right?

461
00:52:30,440 --> 00:52:33,680
But no one gets hurt
as often as you do, Wee.

462
00:52:35,800 --> 00:52:37,200
You're getting used to calling me that.

463
00:52:38,560 --> 00:52:40,920
Who was it that told me

464
00:52:41,000 --> 00:52:42,640
to think of him as an older brother?

465
00:52:47,000 --> 00:52:48,640
So that's all you want me to be?

466
00:52:54,520 --> 00:52:55,360
Uh…

467
00:52:56,720 --> 00:52:57,840
Wait a second.

468
00:53:09,560 --> 00:53:12,320
I just realized this hat belongs to you.

469
00:53:13,000 --> 00:53:15,640
I should've returned it
to its owner long ago.

470
00:53:17,760 --> 00:53:19,000
And

471
00:53:19,760 --> 00:53:21,440
I don't just mean the hat.

472
00:53:22,520 --> 00:53:24,200
I mean the Tayawat name too.

473
00:53:26,520 --> 00:53:28,160
I don't even want it.

474
00:53:29,880 --> 00:53:32,240
It belongs with its rightful owner.

475
00:53:37,800 --> 00:53:38,800
Thank you.

476
00:53:43,080 --> 00:53:44,400
Want me to give you a ride?

477
00:53:45,560 --> 00:53:48,520
No, thanks. Drive safely.

478
00:53:51,520 --> 00:53:52,520
I'll get going, then.

479
00:53:56,840 --> 00:53:57,880
Alyssa.

480
00:54:00,200 --> 00:54:02,640
Call me when you get home, okay?

481
00:55:24,040 --> 00:55:27,240
You don't see me
as just a substitute for Nada, do you?

482
00:55:32,280 --> 00:55:34,000
I don't have feelings for Nada.

483
00:55:44,800 --> 00:55:48,520
She's getting married,
and I don't have anyone.

484
00:55:51,400 --> 00:55:54,040
Could you back me up?

485
00:55:55,200 --> 00:55:56,160
How?

486
00:56:02,920 --> 00:56:05,080
I want revenge on that bastard Prajak.

487
00:56:06,080 --> 00:56:07,680
Please don't stand in my way.

488
00:56:10,720 --> 00:56:14,000
Can you keep it a secret
that Nada and I are twins,

489
00:56:14,080 --> 00:56:16,400
just like our relationship?

490
00:56:21,160 --> 00:56:23,720
You really have been using me all along.

491
00:56:26,840 --> 00:56:28,360
I'm such an idiot.

492
00:56:55,040 --> 00:56:57,000
What exactly are you planning to do?

493
00:56:58,120 --> 00:57:00,360
What about you? What are you planning?

494
00:57:03,840 --> 00:57:04,960
Why did you fake your death?

495
00:57:05,040 --> 00:57:07,120
I had my reasons.

496
00:57:08,440 --> 00:57:11,800
What should I call you then? My nephew?

497
00:57:12,800 --> 00:57:14,160
I don't consider you family.

498
00:57:15,960 --> 00:57:17,080
You killed my mother.

499
00:57:33,240 --> 00:57:35,400
You don't care
whether anyone lives or dies anyway.

500
00:57:35,480 --> 00:57:37,360
Why should I care?

501
00:57:37,440 --> 00:57:40,760
Uncle Thamrong stood by you
through thick and thin,

502
00:57:40,840 --> 00:57:42,720
and you used him until he ended up dead.

503
00:57:42,800 --> 00:57:44,720
He died because of you.

504
00:57:45,440 --> 00:57:46,800
Aren't you going to stop?

505
00:57:47,400 --> 00:57:50,440
Don't you love me anymore, Korn?
Is that why you want me dead?

506
00:57:50,520 --> 00:57:51,480
Wee.

507
00:57:52,000 --> 00:57:54,240
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">I never wanted to be</font></font></i>
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">in this position in the first place.</font></font></i>

508
00:57:54,840 --> 00:57:58,080
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">If I'd known my sacrifice</font></font></i>
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">would turn you into this,</font></font></i>

509
00:57:58,160 --> 00:57:59,800
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">I never would've made that choice.</font></font></i>

510
00:58:01,920 --> 00:58:04,240
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Are you really going to expose Korn?</font></font></i>

511
00:58:05,040 --> 00:58:08,320
To be honest,
I'm starting to have doubts myself.

512
00:58:16,760 --> 00:58:18,120
Don't do this, Korn!

513
00:58:19,080 --> 00:58:20,240
Stay back!

514
00:58:58,640 --> 00:59:01,280
Subtitle translation by:
Chomchanach Yanaharn
